# tools/l/listing_census_witness.rish -- a listing that drops rows names how many.
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES. `tools/fixtures/l/listing_census_scan.sh` reads every tracked `*_scan.sh` under
# `tools/` for a CAPPED LISTING -- a sort piped into head, printed rather than redirected, taking
# more than one row -- and asks whether that file also emits a key naming what it showed or hid.
# The nine ASCII-first meters are a WALL at zero; every other lane ratchets under a ceiling that
# only falls.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS (`20260916.214947`). The nine ASCII-family scans answered `--list` by piping their
# report through `sort -rn | head -40`, and none of the eleven listings said a row had been
# dropped. Across the family 2,972 of 3,321 rows went unprinted in silence -- 89 percent -- while
# seven of the nine headers promised `--list   # name each file and its count`. A reader could not
# tell a row the file never had from a row it dropped, and the reader hurt worst is the one asking
# the narrowest question: eighteen non-ASCII characters stood in five `tools/am/amphora_*`
# witnesses, and this lane read the listing, saw no amphora row, and took it for a clean room.
#
# The class fired twice in one day, which is what turns a repair into a meter: petrichor's
# `seed_link_scan.sh` printed a ratchet site only while its counter stood at or under five, so 847
# sites showed five (`20260916.210332`). A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom.
#
# HOW IT IS PROVEN. `tools/fixtures/l/listing_census_control.sh` builds a real git repository in a
# throwaway pen and plants every reading from both sides -- a silent cap and then its repair, a
# scalar `head -1` and a redirected input bound and a comment naming the shape, each proven NOT to
# count, the family wall and its lift, and the ceiling one over and then at. Four mutations break
# one line of the scan each and assert the leg that must bite actually bites. The control's own leg
# tally is asserted below, so a leg written tomorrow is heard the day it lands. Thirty-eight legs,
# five mutations.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/listing_census_witness.rish

say "listing census: the control, so a green reading below can be believed..."
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/l/listing_census_control.sh"]
if control.ok == false then say control.err
assert control.ok else "listing_census: the control refused to run -- read the line above"

assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "listing_census: the control found a planted case it could not read"

# A control's own verdict says only that it reached its last line. The leg tally says how much of
# it was heard, so a leg written tomorrow is asserted rather than silently added.
assert control.out contains "control_legs=38" else "listing_census: the control's leg count moved -- read it and update this number"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "listing_census: a control leg failed -- run the control and read its FAILED lines"

say "listing census: the living tree..."
let live = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/l/listing_census_scan.sh"]
if live.ok == false then say live.err
assert live.ok else "listing_census: the scan refused the tree -- read the line above"

assert live.out contains "instrument=ok" else "listing_census: the scan could not read its own population"

# The wall. The nine ASCII meters were repaired on the lap this guard was seated, so the next
# silent cap added to one of them reds on the lap it arrives.
assert live.out contains "family_walled=yes" else "listing_census: an ASCII-family listing caps its rows and does not say so -- sh tools/fixtures/l/listing_census_scan.sh --list"

# The ratchet. Thirteen caps across nine files stand in nine other lanes; each falls when its own
# lane touches it, and the ceiling falls with it.
assert live.out contains "under_ceiling=yes" else "listing_census: uncensused caps rose above the ceiling -- sh tools/fixtures/l/listing_census_scan.sh --list"

assert live.out contains "verdict=ok" else "listing_census: the scan refused the tree -- read its --list"

say "GREEN: listing census -- every ASCII-family listing names what it dropped, and the rest stand under a falling ceiling."
